From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:55:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: fheroes2$AudioRate to choose the sound output rate

The output rate stays 44100 Hz. fheroes2$AudioRate 22050 (or 11025,
48000) changes it: at 22050 Hz the MIDI synthesiser and the mixing do
half the work (the game's sound effects are 22050 Hz anyway; the music
loses its top octave), as fheroes2 does on the PS Vita. The buffer
keeps about the same length in time.
---
 src/engine/audio.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/engine/audio.cpp b/src/engine/audio.cpp
index be9cd7c..9018128 100644
--- a/src/engine/audio.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/audio.cpp
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include "audio.h"
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <atomic>
 #include <cassert>
 #include <cmath>
@@ -656,7 +657,21 @@ void Audio::Init()
         }
     }
 
+#if defined( __riscos__ )
+    // RISC OS: fheroes2$AudioRate 22050 halves the work of the MIDI synthesiser and of the
+    // mixing (the game's sound effects are 22050 Hz anyway; music loses its top octave).
+    AudioSpec audioSpec;
+    if ( const char * rate = getenv( "fheroes2$AudioRate" ); rate != nullptr ) {
+        const int frequency = atoi( rate );
+        if ( frequency == 11025 || frequency == 22050 || frequency == 44100 || frequency == 48000 ) {
+            // Keep the buffer about the same length in time.
+            audioSpec.chunkSize = std::max( 1024, audioSpec.chunkSize * frequency / 44100 / 1024 * 1024 );
+            audioSpec.frequency = frequency;
+        }
+    }
+#else
     const AudioSpec audioSpec;
+#endif
 
     if ( Mix_OpenAudio( audioSpec.frequency, audioSpec.format, audioSpec.channels, audioSpec.chunkSize ) != 0 ) {
         ERROR_LOG( "Failed to initialize an audio device. The error: " << Mix_GetError() )
